WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.000
An Ingress, a Service, a
Deployment, a network policy.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.447
Every object is there.

3
00:00:05.447 --> 00:00:07.682
Does a request ever reach the pod?

4
00:00:08.883 --> 00:00:10.032
So walk the path.

5
00:00:10.032 --> 00:00:12.126
kube-noob grades it hop by hop.

6
00:00:13.383 --> 00:00:16.725
6 hops hold, and each names
the rules that read it.

7
00:00:16.725 --> 00:00:20.068
The last hop, across the
node, no manifest records.

8
00:00:20.068 --> 00:00:23.410
It is not checked, and it
is not counted as passed.

9
00:00:24.616 --> 00:00:28.784
Point the Ingress at a retired
controller, and that hop is broken.

10
00:00:28.784 --> 00:00:32.573
The walk names the rule, still
reaches the end, and exits 1.

11
00:00:33.783 --> 00:00:36.967
Now pass one file instead
of the whole namespace.

12
00:00:36.967 --> 00:00:41.450
The policy hop cannot be judged, so
the walk stops there and exits 5.

13
00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:43.724
The 2 hops after it are not walked.

14
00:00:44.916 --> 00:00:46.216
That is the whole rule.

15
00:00:46.216 --> 00:00:49.439
A hop nothing read is never
reported as a hop that works.

16
00:00:52.416 --> 00:00:55.040
Walk the path your own manifests describe.

17
00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:56.789
Get it at kube-noob dot com.
